  <sharedProfiles>
    <profile name="Advanced Energy Shielding" id="641e-5c80-ab9c-df38" hidden="false" typeId="d4b8-6c36-8bad-c884" typeName="Wargear Item">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1cc-ea5e-6a1d-d78e">A model with this upgrade benefits from enhanced shielding and reinforced armor systems. There combat harness may be more advanced or of superior make to those around them. 


While the model has any remaining wounds allocated to its Energy Shielding, it gains +1 to its Toughness for the purposes of resolving To Wound rolls and other effects that use the model&apos;s Toughness characteristic.


This bonus is lost immediately once the model has no remaining Energy Shielding wounds</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Energy Shielding" id="62ee-6610-ca13-96b4" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model is allocated a Wound, it instead suffers the wound to it&apos;s energy shielding. This model may take as many wounds to it&apos;s Energy Shielding each turn as are equal to the number in brackets associated with the specific varient of this special rule, for example (Energy Shielding 2) would infer two wounds allocated to Energy Shielding before the target model is wounded directly. 
Energy Shielding regenerates by 1 at the start of each battleround to it&apos;s maximum value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Covenant Plasma" id="33ee-bac7-9e15-e729" hidden="false">
      <description>Negate the effects of any &quot;Shielding&quot; based special rules that are the target of this weapon. Reduces Invulnurable Saves by 1</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Honour Before All Else" id="d010-195e-920c-a640" hidden="false">
      <description>An Elite may never refuse a challenge. In additon, any unit with an Elite in it always rolls leadership without modifiers for the purpose of morale checks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grunt Fodder" id="4fcd-c0af-1d5e-a146" hidden="false">
      <description>When a Grunt&apos;s Squad Leader is destroyed, this unit must immediatly make a leadership check. On a failed Leadership check, D6 Grunts immediatly attempt to charge D6 inches towards the closest enemy unit. These models then explode with the plasma grenade weapon profile, regardless of if they hit their target or not.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combined Explosion" id="f27a-4b30-bdbf-d247" hidden="false">
      <description>This weapon gains the Instant Death special rule on a To Wound roll of 6+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tracking Needles" id="b220-402d-837e-fb9e" hidden="false">
      <description>When targeting a model within half range of the needler, add +1 to hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bond Brothers" id="5294-6290-ace2-e98b" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Hunter from a Hunter pack is destroyed, the remaining Hunter gains Hatred for the unit which destroyed the first Hunter. In addition, the remaining Hunter gains Rage (2) and Rampage (2)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hunter Pack" id="7d8b-d7be-18fd-e805" hidden="false">
      <description>No model or unit may join a Hunter Pack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battlelust" id="1fe5-d2e9-2ce0-0464" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of a Charge declared by a unit which includes a model with the Battlelust (x) special roll roll a Leadership test.

If the test is passed, resolve the Charge as normal.

If the test is failed, any models within the unit which contain the Battlelust (x) special rule immedietly drops all carried Ranged weapons (they may not use any Ranged weapons for the rest of the battle). However, these models gain the Rage (X) and Furious Charge (X) special rules for the remainder of the battle where X is the number listed in the Battlelust rule.


In addition, a model, and any unit they are apart of, under the effects of Battlelust must always Consolidate toward the nearest visible enemy, and must declare a Charge if one is possible in each following Assault Phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Volatile Overcharge" id="4c6b-91d1-0ce3-2c33" hidden="false">
      <description>Brute Plasma Rifles are notoriously unstable. Their overcharged capacitors give them incredible firepower, but risk burning out entirely.


After resolving all shots made with this weapon, roll a D6. On a roll of 1, the weapon overheats and may not be fired during the next Shooting Phase. Place a token or mark the model to indicate the weapon is disabled.


The model may choose to fire an Overheated weapon regardless. If it chooses to do so, it immediately suffers a wound with no saves of any kind allowed and the weapon remains overheated for the following turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Engineer" id="2a03-a3e7-fb99-1018" hidden="false">
      <description>In each of your Shooting phases, a Huragok can choose to repair a single friendly vehicle that it is in base contact with or embarked upon. To repair a vehicle, roll a D6 and add 1 for each Huragok in base contact with the vehicle. If the result is a 5 or more, you may either restore a Hull Point lost earlier in the battle, or repair a Weapon Destroyed or Immobilised result suffered earlier in the battle; this is effective immediately. Each Huragok in base contact may also attempt this roll and recieve the benefits of each other Huragok in base contact.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cluster" id="3d50-e666-d4df-4882" hidden="false">
      <description>A Cluster of Huragok may split off from each other and join other units.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="State of Grace" id="0fb1-da27-a45c-c70f" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit that includes one or more Huragok with this special rule increases its Energy Shielding by +1. If a model did not have an Energy Shield, it instead gains Energy Shielding (1).

This bonus does not stack with itself — a unit may only benefit from one instance of State of Grace at any time, regardless of how many Huragok are attached to it.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lunge" id="ea4b-19bc-28de-06f8" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with an Energy sword may add +2 to it&apos;s charge value. On the first round of combat, add +1 to the attacks characteristic of a model with this weapon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dazzling Light" id="7634-31a5-a2a5-a2d7" hidden="false">
      <description>Models affected by the blast from a Flare must reduce their Initiative by 1 until the end of their next turn, and must then take a Blind test. This modifier stacks with any other Initiative modifiers but cannot reduce a model’s Initiative below 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Restorative Field" id="5cff-d2fd-4d6d-6c74" hidden="false">
      <description>After placing the Blast Marker from the Regenerator, leave it in place until the end of the next turn. Any non-vehicle models within the blast marker gain the Feel No Pain (5+) special rule. If a model already has a Feel No Pain roll, use the better of the two values.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shield Disruption" id="6dca-5600-6298-03c1" hidden="false">
      <description>After placing the Blast Marker from the Power Drain, leave it in place until the end of the next turn. Any models within the blast marker suffer a -1 penalty to all Invulnurable Saves (To a minimum of 6+) until the end of their next turn. Any vehicles within the blast marker are unable to move. In addition, if a model has the Energy Shielding special rule, it may not regenerate Energy Shielding so long as it remains inside the blast marker.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Grunt Squad" id="f600-c88f-4166-4d69" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink name="Plasma Grenade" id="c2f9-a589-9e67-4dfa" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="2b86-00e1-892e-3090" type="selectionEntry"/>
      </entryLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Unggoy Tactics" id="5486-6b35-c9d6-171c" hidden="false">
          <description>At the start of your Movement phase, a Grunt Squad may split into smaller detachments. Any number of 5-model groups within the unit may break off and join a different friendly unit within unit coherency, so long as the unit they are joining contains at least one Elite, Brute, or Grunt Ultra and does not contain any Elite Zealot models.


Once joined, these detachments are treated as part of their new unit for all rules purposes (including coherency, morale, and targeting).


A Grunt Squad may only split in this way if:
– It is not locked in combat,
– All models involved are currently on the battlefield, and
– The original Grunt Squad retains at least 10 models, including its Squad Leader, after any detachments are made.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
