          <profiles>
            <profile name="Ghost" id="56e7-65a6-0db4-6087" hidden="false" typeId="35bb-3fdd-dd9d-1fc8" typeName="Unit">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="2ba2-3a82-dfb7-7849">Bike(AntiGrav)</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="M" typeId="e8fa-a6b3-0e8c-18aa">14&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="9660-0df5-9c5d-3604">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="565d-bf36-9e7e-29b5">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="23ae-6026-aebd-abc3">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="f6db-a6a5-71d2-71c5">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="a763-cbc8-2080-a4fb">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="ea41-893b-3f82-5482">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="d535-b745-b613-a7ab">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="3b5e-ab67-ed36-a88f">7</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="d33e-1fdc-0c00-8cb8">3+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="3df9-f556-8725-fe75">Hammer of Wrath (1), Relentless, Bulky (2), Hit and Run</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Gravity Boost" id="0874-ca8b-8019-1717" hidden="false">
              <description>Ghosts cannot Run, but can make a special gravity-boost move instead of firing in their Shooting phase.

At the beginning of the movement phase, declare which Ghosts will make a Gravity Boost move. Ghosts may rotate up to 90&quot; before moving. A Gravity Boosted ghost moves up to double it&apos;s movement speed charactistic in a straight line and may not fire it&apos;s weapons this turn.

Splatter: A Gravity boosting Ghost may choose to charge a model in the charge phase, using it&apos;s boosted movement charactistic. If it does so, it resolves Hammer of Wrath rolls at Strength 6 AP2</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Gravity Propulsion Drive" id="6ee2-6f56-7eb0-7093" hidden="false">
              <description>The Ghost&apos;s Gravity drives allow it to hover over terrain. Ghosts gain the Antigrav subtype as well as the Hit and Run Special Rule. However, a Ghost may not make Jink rolls like regular Bike units. 

If a Ghost is destroyed it explodes. Nearby units suffer a Strength 4 AP- Hit for each model within D6&quot; of the Ghosts base and any unit that suffers one or more Hits from this effect must take an immediate single Pinning test. Once all Hits and Pinning tests are resolved, the Ghost is then removed from the battlefield.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Class 2 Energy-Gun" id="6cbd-f4b7-65e8-9e0a" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="43e0-35d7-9cb8-02e6" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="2"/>
